      "title": "Pollution load falls along the train",
      "description": "Screening removes rags and grit; equalisation evens out flow and strength; neutralisation brings pH into the ≈ 6–9 range the bacteria tolerate. In the aeration tank bacteria oxidise dissolved organic matter (BOD/COD) using oxygen from the diffusers (DO ≈ 1.5–2 mg/L), growing into flocs. The clarifier settles the flocs: most are returned (RAS) to keep the biomass (MLSS ≈ 2,000–4,000 mg/L), the growth is wasted (WAS), and clear treated effluent leaves over the weir — typically > 90 % BOD removal. Discharge limits are set by the local regulator.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
